# CSS structure

Route styles live in `src/css/`, one file per route. The filename is the lowercase route slug.

- `/` → `src/css/home.css`
- `/about` → `src/css/about.css`
- `/services` → `src/css/services.css`
- UI used on more than one route (`.navbar`, `.button`) → `src/css/shared.css`

`src/index.css` stays `@import "tailwindcss";` and `@theme` tokens only. Each file in `src/css/` starts with `@reference "tailwindcss";`. The page imports its route file. The shell imports `shared.css` once.

Each UI part is one kebab-case class. Tailwind utilities go in `@apply`. JSX uses that class name only.

```css
.navbar {
  @apply border-b border-zinc-200 bg-white;
}

.home-hero {
  @apply mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-16;
}
```

- Page-only classes start with the route slug: `.home-hero`, `.services-card`
- Children extend the parent name: `.navbar-link`, `.navbar-link-active`
- Shared components use the component name: `.navbar`, `.button-secondary`

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<header className="border-b border-zinc-200 bg-white">

// ✅ GOOD
<header className="navbar">
```

Do not put route classes in `src/index.css` or in a component file. Do not use camelCase, PascalCase, or utility-like names (`.flex-center`). Do not copy a shared class into every route file.
